# Concept drawings

When a concept is easier to see than to read, add one fine-line stick-figure drawing under the opening, before the technical sections. Photos, overlays, and charts stay where they are.

Style, every time: white background, thin black pen, no shading, no gray fill, no color, no logos. One idea. Labels must match the facts.

```markdown
# ❌ The label invents a geometry
A ship in DOTA is eight corners.

# ✅ Four points, eight numbers
A ship in DOTA is four corners, written as eight coordinates.
```

Save the file in `content/posts/img/` and embed it so the alt text is the one-line caption the theme prints underneath:

```markdown
![Four corners, eight coordinates, become a center, a long side, a short side, and one angle.](/posts/img/2026-10-19_sketch_le90.jpg#layoutTextWidth)
```
